 INPUT CARD>! aa001a: PURIFY not set at all -- trans/rot frequencies contaminated.          
 INPUT CARD>! aa001b: added STATPT PURIFY=.T. -- made essentially no difference             
 INPUT CARD>! (changes under 2 cm-1, pure numerical noise). Checked $FORCE's own            
 INPUT CARD>! documentation directly: PURIFY is ALSO a separate $FORCE keyword,             
 INPUT CARD>! specifically responsible for cleaning up the FINAL Hessian/frequency          
 INPUT CARD>! output from HSSEND -- "(default=.FALSE. if $ZMAT is given)". STATPT's         
 INPUT CARD>! PURIFY only affects the Hessian used internally during the search             
 INPUT CARD>! itself, not the final HSSEND analysis. This also retroactively explains       
 INPUT CARD>! why the chloroacetaldehyde work never needed this: those runs used            
